{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-57136","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66005","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-57137","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66006","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66007","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-66008","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-66009","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-66010","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-66011","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-66012","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-66013","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-57138","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-57140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66014","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-57141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66015","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-57142","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66016","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-57143","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66017","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-57145","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66018","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-57147","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66019","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-57149","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66020","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-57151","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66021","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-57153","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66022","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-57155","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66023","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-57157","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57160","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66024","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-57159","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66025","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57162","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66026","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-57163","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66027","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-66028","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-66029","text":". You declare *rooms* (tiles), *claims* (file-system regions each room owns), *neighbors* (adjacency for navigation), and *state bindings* (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-57164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66030","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-66031","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-66032","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-57165","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66033","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-57166","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66034","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-66035","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-66036","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-66037","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-57167","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66038","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-66039","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-57169","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66040","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-66041","text":" Apps add *vocabularies* (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-66042","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-66043","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66044","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-66045","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66046","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-66047","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-57171","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66048","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-66049","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-57173","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57175","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66050","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-57176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66051","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-57177","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66052","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-57178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66053","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-57179","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-57180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66054","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-66055","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66056","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-66057","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-66058","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-66059","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-66060","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-66061","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-57181","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66062","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-57182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66063","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-66064","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-66065","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66066","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-66067","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66068","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-66069","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-57183","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-57184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66070","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-66071","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-66072","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-66073","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-57185","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66074","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-57186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66075","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-66076","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-66077","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-57187","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-57188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66078","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-66079","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-66080","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-66081","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-66082","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-66083","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-66084","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-66085","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-57189","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66086","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-57190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66087","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the *binding*, not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-57191","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-57192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66088","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-66089","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-66090","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-66091","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66092","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-66093","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66094","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-66095","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66096","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-66097","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66098","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-66099","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-66100","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-66101","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-57193","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66102","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-57194","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66103","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-66104","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-66105","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-57195","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-57196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66106","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-66107","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66108","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-66109","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-66110","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-66111","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-66112","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-66113","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-57197","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66114","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-57198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66115","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-66116","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-66117","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-57199","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-57200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66118","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-57201","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-57202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66119","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-57203","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66120","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-57204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66121","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-57205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66122","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-66123","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-66124","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-66125","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-66126","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66127","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-66128","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable. 2. "},{"id":"spn-66129","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-66130","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-66131","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-66132","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior. 3. "},{"id":"spn-66133","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-66134","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-66135","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-66136","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-66137","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-66138","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66139","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-66140","text":", etc. 4. "},{"id":"spn-66141","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-66142","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-66143","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-66144","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-66145","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-66146","text":"). 5. "},{"id":"spn-66147","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-66148","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-66149","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-66150","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-66151","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-66152","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]},{"id":"blk-57206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66153","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-57207","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66154","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-66155","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-66156","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-57208","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66157","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-57210","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66158","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-57212","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66159","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-57215","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66160","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-57216","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66161","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-66162","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-66163","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-57218","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66164","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-57220","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66165","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-66166","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-66167","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66168","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-66169","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66170","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-66171","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-57222","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57224","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66172","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-57225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66173","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a *vocabulary* — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-66174","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-66175","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-57226","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-57227","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66176","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-66177","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-66178","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-66179","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-66180","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-66181","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-66182","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-66183","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-57228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66184","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-57229","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66185","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-66186","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-57230","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66187","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-66188","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-57232","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66189","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-66190","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-57234","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57237","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66191","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-66192","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-57236","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57238","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66193","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-66194","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-66195","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-57239","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66196","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-57240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66197","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-57241","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57243","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66198","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-66199","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-57242","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66200","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-66201","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-57244","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57247","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66202","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-66203","text":" That's a *vocabulary* ("},{"id":"spn-66204","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-66205","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-57246","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66206","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-66207","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-57248","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57251","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66208","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-66209","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-66210","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-66211","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-57250","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57252","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66212","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-57253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66213","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-66214","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-66215","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-57254","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66216","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-66217","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-57255","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66218","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-66219","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-57257","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66220","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-66221","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-57259","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66222","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-57262","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66223","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-66224","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-57263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66225","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-66226","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-66227","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-66228","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-66229","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66230","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-66231","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66232","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-66233","text":", "},{"id":"spn-66234","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-66235","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-66236","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-66237","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-57264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66238","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-57265","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66239","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-66240","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-66241","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-66242","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-57266","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66243","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-66244","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-57268","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66245","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-66246","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-66247","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-66248","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-57270","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66249","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-66250","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-66251","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-57273","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66252","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-57274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66253","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-57276","spans":[{"id":"spn-66254","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-57277","spans":[{"id":"spn-66255","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-57278","spans":[{"id":"spn-66256","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-57275","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-57279","spans":[{"id":"spn-66257","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-57280","spans":[{"id":"spn-66258","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-57281","spans":[{"id":"spn-66259","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57282","spans":[{"id":"spn-66260","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-66261","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-57283","spans":[{"id":"spn-66262","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-57284","spans":[{"id":"spn-66263","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-57285","spans":[{"id":"spn-66264","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-66265","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-57286","spans":[{"id":"spn-66266","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-57287","spans":[{"id":"spn-66267","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-57288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66268","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-66269","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-66270","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-57289","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66271","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-57290","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-57291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66272","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-57292","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66273","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-57293","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66274","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-66275","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-66276","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-66277","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-66278","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact. 2. Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-66279","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-66280","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo. 3. CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-66281","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-66282","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-66283","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-66284","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-66285","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-66286","text":" → static HTML. 4. Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]},{"id":"blk-57294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66287","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-57295","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66288","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-57296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66289","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-66290","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-66291","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-57297","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66292","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-66293","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-66294","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-66295","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-66296","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-66297","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-57298","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57301","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66298","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-57300","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66299","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-57302","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66300","text":"These are *integration patterns*, not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-57305","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-66301","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-57306","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66302","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-66303","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-57307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66304","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-66305","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-57309","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66306","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-66307","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-66308","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-66309","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-57311","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-57314","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66310","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-66311","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-57313","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-57315","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66312","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-57316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66313","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-57317","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-66314","text":"*This spec is the contract. Everything in "},{"id":"spn-66315","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-66316","text":" (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the "},{"id":"spn-66317","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-66318","text":" vocabulary plus the "},{"id":"spn-66319","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dark_factory"},{"id":"spn-66320","text":" reference application — both built on top of this protocol.*"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraqc7mu5ol2xtyqxnj4q4vabbillp2sop7likbtoukuhey7l3pcaiq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}